At 2:30 am on Labor Day, I finished a frustrated labor of ascension. The 
RNG chose to be extremely stingy:
- I did not have magic resistance until my first wish in the Castle.
- Multiple thrones only provided genocide of cockatrices
- only one scroll of genocide for the Lich family
- 2 large shops of hardware full of bags, chests, boxes, and tin 
openers, not much useful
- only two wands of teleportation in the entire dungeon

I will skip the usual summary. Lessons learned:
1. Don't fire arrows of unknown BUC status from the front door of the a 
temple with a (co-aligned) priest inside. One cursed arrow into the orc; 
three into the priest. I had to finish the priest off to get may stash back.
2. Poisoned arrows are very useful in the most interesting situations.
3. Don't get rid of your backup source of reflection; Rodney will steal 
your primary reflection item. Then, you will watch all your wands and 
rings disappear in bright explosions from lightning. The RNG only 
provided 2 wands of teleportation; Moloch's minions gave me 2 less.
4. Don't carry a wand of digging in your inventory when making "the 
run". Rodney will steal the wand; and you get to chase Rodney down 9 
levels till the wand runs out.
5. Don't forget, next time, to put on your ring of +3 consitution when 
you level up multiples times with potions of gain level.
6. Training to Expert with a boomerang is tedious; and still an 
unfulfilled goal.
7. The RNG can be very stingy.
8. Don't wait till the last minute to use a wish on a ring of conflict. 
If the RNG is stingy, waiting won't "make it so".
9. Luck is better than skill; found the altar on my first choice.
10.  Better to have a half dozen arrows degraded by a disenchanter than 
Stormbringer. Stormy was at +0 when I ascended.
11. Don't try to be tricky when Yeenaghou shows up -- just kill him. 
Cost me my only amulet of life saving; and convinced me to burn a wish 
on GDSM.

Although not trying to maintain conducts, failure of the RNG to provide 
left me polyless, polyselfless, and I did not wish for any artifacts (I 
needed basics).


